1
00:00:09,870 --> 00:00:15,870
This video demonstrates the donning and doffing of the following PPE.

2
00:00:15,870 --> 00:00:22,870
Laboratory coats, gloves, and safety glasses with wraparound sides.

3
00:00:22,870 --> 00:00:33,870
The first step is to remove personal items such as jewelry, watches, coats, jackets, cell phones, pens, or additional bags,

4
00:00:33,870 --> 00:00:38,870
and place them in a location outside of the laboratory.

5
00:00:38,870 --> 00:00:42,870
Then, tie back any long hair if present.

6
00:00:42,870 --> 00:00:51,870
Next, gather your laboratory coat with tight cuffs, gloves, and safety glasses with wraparound sides.

7
00:00:51,870 --> 00:00:55,870
Make sure you have the right size laboratory coat and gloves,

8
00:00:55,870 --> 00:01:03,870
and don't forget to visually inspect all of your PPE for rips, tears, or missing snaps.

9
00:01:03,870 --> 00:01:08,870
Next, put on the laboratory coat and snap it completely.

10
00:01:08,870 --> 00:01:15,870
Then, put on your safety glasses, and finally, put on your gloves.

11
00:01:15,870 --> 00:01:21,870
There are various strategies for establishing the sequence of doffing PPE.

12
00:01:21,870 --> 00:01:29,870
The strategy demonstrated in this video is to remove PPE from most contaminated to least contaminated.

13
00:01:29,870 --> 00:01:36,870
To doff your PPE, the first step is to slowly and gently remove your gloves.

14
00:01:36,870 --> 00:01:41,870
Start by making an L with your thumb and first finger.

15
00:01:41,870 --> 00:01:46,870
Then, place your fingers perpendicular to your wrist and pinch.

16
00:01:46,870 --> 00:01:51,870
Be careful to not touch the cuff of the coat with your dirty glove.

17
00:01:51,870 --> 00:01:54,870
Next, pull the glove completely off.

18
00:01:54,870 --> 00:01:57,870
It should now be inside out.

19
00:01:57,870 --> 00:02:03,870
Grab the inside-out glove with your bare hand, the one the glove just came off of,

20
00:02:03,870 --> 00:02:07,870
and then pinch the other glove at the wrist.

21
00:02:07,870 --> 00:02:12,870
Then, pull the pinched glove up high and away from the wrist.

22
00:02:12,870 --> 00:02:17,870
Pull the glove off, making sure the gloved hand is flat

23
00:02:17,870 --> 00:02:22,870
and you do not touch the outside of the contaminated glove with your clean hand.

24
00:02:22,870 --> 00:02:27,870
And last, discard the gloves into the biohazard waste container.

25
00:02:27,870 --> 00:02:31,870
Remember, do not reuse the gloves.

26
00:02:31,870 --> 00:02:39,870
Take care to not touch the potentially contaminated outside surfaces of your laboratory coat with your bare hands.

27
00:02:39,870 --> 00:02:46,870
The cuffs of the coat should be clean, however, as the gloves extended over them during your work.

28
00:02:46,870 --> 00:02:55,870
Next, unsnap your laboratory coat and grasp the sleeve cuff of one of the arms and pull off the laboratory coat.

29
00:02:55,870 --> 00:02:58,870
Do the same for the other arm.

30
00:02:58,870 --> 00:03:05,870
If you are reusing the laboratory coat, hang the laboratory coat in a designated area.

31
00:03:05,870 --> 00:03:12,870
Please note, if there is visible contamination or it is determined that the laboratory coat should be disposed of,

32
00:03:12,870 --> 00:03:15,870
with the inside of the coat facing towards you,

33
00:03:15,870 --> 00:03:20,870
fold the coat away from you and roll it inside out into a bundle,

34
00:03:20,870 --> 00:03:24,870
then dispose of it in the biohazard waste container.

35
00:03:24,870 --> 00:03:30,870
Next, remove your safety glasses by grasping the frames at the temples.

36
00:03:30,870 --> 00:03:35,870
This is an area where there is less potential for contamination.

37
00:03:35,870 --> 00:03:40,870
Place them in a designated area to be disinfected at the end of the shift.

38
00:03:40,870 --> 00:03:47,870
Remember to use gloves and cleaning products that meet the EPA's approval to clean your safety glasses

39
00:03:47,870 --> 00:03:51,870
and follow the manufacturer's recommendations for contact time.

40
00:03:51,870 --> 00:03:55,870
Last, wash your hands with soap and water.

41
00:03:55,870 --> 00:04:03,870
Lather the backs of your hands, between your fingers and under your nails, and scrub for at least 20 seconds.

42
00:04:03,870 --> 00:04:12,870
An alcohol-based hand sanitizer containing at least 60% ethanol or 70% isopropanol

43
00:04:12,870 --> 00:04:17,870
can be used as a temporary solution until soap and water are available.

44
00:04:17,870 --> 00:04:20,870
Additional considerations

45
00:04:20,870 --> 00:04:26,870
Closed-toed shoes with solid and impermeable uppers should be worn in the laboratory.

46
00:04:26,870 --> 00:04:33,870
PPE will vary based on laboratory-specific and procedure-specific risk assessments.

47
00:04:33,870 --> 00:04:38,870
Donning and doffing areas should be physically separated from each other

48
00:04:38,870 --> 00:04:45,870
to avoid contamination of clean PPE and personal belongings with potentially contaminated PPE.

49
00:04:45,870 --> 00:04:49,870
Donning and doffing procedures vary per institution.

50
00:04:49,870 --> 00:04:53,870
Follow your institutional policies and procedures.

51
00:04:54,870 --> 00:05:02,870
For additional training and workforce development resources, please visit cdc.gov slash labtraining

52
00:05:02,870 --> 00:05:05,870
and click on the Job Aids button.
